=> free shows RAM and swap memory usage.

=> Basic command:

free

Better:

free -h

=> Example:

              total   used   free   shared  buff/cache  available
Mem:           8.0G   3.2G   1.5G     200M       3.3G       4.4G
Swap:          2.0G   100M   1.9G

=> Important columns:

total → Total RAM
used → RAM currently being used
free → Completely unused RAM
buff/cache → RAM being used for cache/buffers
available → Approximate RAM available for new applications

=> Common command
free -h

=> You use this when troubleshooting:

"Server RAM is high."
